{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/143838-paper-tigers","id":143838,"title":"Paper Tigers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-20T14:00:29-07:00","id":143838,"title":"Paper Tigers","content":"<i>(a menacing growl coupled with the sounds of crinkling paper)</i><br /> <br /> They'd be a peculiar hobgoblin of there were any hobgoblins that aren't. Paper Tigers are the embodiment of political manipulation and tissue-thin lies. They're scary unless you're scarier, and any king, bishop, or princess can strike them down with ease. They're more of a nuisance than anything, but in freeholds in which they gather, they can sow discord and distrust that can tear fragile Lost communities apart.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Paper Tigers are about the size and shape of actual tigers, only, unsurprisingly enough, made out of paper. Specifically, they seem to be composed of manila construction paper folded into the shape of an origami-style tiger, complete with crayon-colored stripes. Speculation into their origin usually tends toward escapees of the dreams of corrupt politicians, though they are also rumored to have some sort of connection to either one of two True Fae: the Scribbling Prince (a precocious, eternal toddler whose magic crayons bring drawings to life), or the Dandy Lion (a nearly comical bipedal cat with a mortal fear of francophones).<br /> <br /> <b>Monstrous Aspects<br /> <br /> Scaredy Cat:</b> Paper Tigers are indeed quite tiger-like, to the point where they share stats with their more mundane cousins in the World of Darkness. However, their true nature is revealed to anyone who has mastered fear. Against anyone with at least three dots in Intimidate, Autumn Mantle, or Fleeting Autumn, a Paper Tiger's attacks only inflict a single point of Bashing damage. It's like being mauled by a cardboard box and frankly is a little embarrassing for everyone involved.<br /> <br /> <b>Made of Paper:</b> Attacks made against Paper Tigers that utilize water (such as with the Contracts of Elements) always deal Lethal damage. If a water-based attack would deal Lethal damage, it deals Aggravated instead. If it would ordinarily deal Aggravated damage, well, aren't you special? A Paper Tiger caught in a rainstorm takes one point of Bashing damage per minute, and one submerged in water suffers a point every turn. Fire-based attacks that hit always cause the Paper Tiger to catch fire.<br /> <br /> <b>Paste Trophy:</b> Like any manifestation of the Wyrd, a Paper Tiger's nature is threefold. Its name comes first from the fact that it is literally a tiger made of paper, secondly because though initially menacing, they don't actually pose much of a threat. Physically anyway. There's one more aspect to a Paper Tiger: If a piece of a dead Paper Tiger is removed from the body, and a certain ritual is enacted over it (ask a witch, they probably know), the paper transforms into physical evidence of an enemy vanquished. It might be the head of a Fae lord, a serial killer's beloved bloodstained hunting knife, or a signed confession of Loyalism from a deceased changeling. All the details are in order, and no amount of scrutiny will reveal the fake, though, obviously, a supposedly-dead individual showing up at the Midwinter Ball will poke some holes in your story. Also, trying to pass off a Paper Tiger as real evidence is a Clarity-7 Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> <b>Story Hooks</b><br /> <br /> No one knows what's worse in this town anymore: the Summer King's increasingly-brash claims to ferret out Loyalist scum in the Freehold, or the Winter King's increasingly-odd reclusiveness, disappearing for weeks on end to God-knows where. Then, one day at a Court gathering, the Monarch of High Noon grimly produces a tape, on which the Lord of the Forbidding Tundra confesses to his crimes and makes a solemn vow to leave and never return. Except, just the other day someone saw the two kings meeting in (supposed) secret, acting quite amicable with each other, despite the fronts of public animosity both have always put on. Something's not right here, and someone's planning something. What's really going on here? Is there even an actual Loyalist plot?<br /> <br /> Everyone in the Autumn Court knows about Paper Tigers. Being a Baron of the Lesser Ones, you helped write the book on them. Scylla did too, which is why everyone is more than a little surprised when she shows up one day with the head of the Jackdaw, an infamous Privateer who's terrorized the Freehold for over a decade. There's no way she single-handedly took him out, and with the recent feline infestation in the Hedge, even her hard physical evidence is pretty suspect. Scylla has always seemed to teeter on the edge of madness; maybe she's finally tipped over. Plus, her time-frame is all wrong. While she was away, Ser Clermont and Madame Clementine claim they found the Jackdaw's calling card\u2014three raven feathers pasted to a browned oak leaf\u2014in their private Hollow. Of course, it's possible she's being set up by someone who doesn't want the Jackdaw's legacy to die out just yet, using the Paper Tigers as a convenient cover. But who would want that?<br /> <br /> At first the Paper Tigers started showing up in the Hedge, and you all just ignored them. Then came the Paper Wolves. Weird, but same principle, right? After that were the Paper Deer, the Paper Crocodiles, the Paper Hawks.... The whole local Hedge is now one big Paper Fucking Zoo. What the hell? You don't think...could it be the Scribbling Prince?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}